  "case_for": "A solo builder with AI agents can ship a working MVP fast: the core mechanics (ingest JUnit/test-history data, correlate failures with code-change scope, flag statistically flaky tests, recommend a minimal blocking test subset) are already proven out by multiple tiny open-source/indie projects (ci-sherlock-agent, flaketriage, ai-flake-sleuth, flaky-detector-agent) built by individuals, showing the technical lift is within reach of a one-person team. Distribution has a near-zero-cost channel in GitHub Marketplace/CI marketplaces, and the pain is well documented and widely felt (Trunk's analysis of 20.2M CI jobs, multiple r/programming threads) across teams too small to justify Develocity's or Harness's enterprise contracts, leaving room for a cheap, fast, self-serve wedge priced below the enterprise incumbents.",
